# Add IA agent support

General idea: You will create a plan for adding IA-agent-based suggestions into the main editor of
the matchbox application. This includes:
- in order to select the IA agent, I would like you to create a modal window, that can be
called from the file menu, for selecting a model. This will be in the
matchbox-gui submodule. The window will offer to select Claude or ChatGPT and to
add their API keys. It will also offer to use Ollama for free weight model.
- You will add the dependencies to the corresponding maven artifact in the pom.xml
file of matchbox-gui submodule.
- In the main text editor of the application, you
will add suggestion returned by the selected agent. suggestions will appears as grey text
in the editor.

- What I would like to achieve is that the AI agent could take into account
which grammars have been selected for the file currently edited in order to
include suggestions that format the text according to this grammar. Indeed, in
each project, files are associated with one or several grammars (the submodule
in the grammars/ directory) that will match portions of the text. If you need
the grammar contract (as defined in the matchbox-grammar-api module) to be
changed in order to have more information that could be given to the prompt, for
instance the antlr grammar or a description of the rule, please suggest such
modifications.

If you have suggestions about what could be added to the plan, how to improve
it, or architectural change that would importe it, please suggest such
modifications.


could you please make a plan to improve the settings mechanism that is in the
ApplicationSettings class in the matchbox-app module. I would like the ApplicationSettings
class to be refactored to use a more modern settings mechanism and to write settings
in the standard location of each OS.

